1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:03,250
Let's set up the game together, one step at a time.

2
00:00:04,266 --> 00:00:06,122
Each player takes a player board.

3
00:00:06,442 --> 00:00:09,450
Everyone uses the same side: the coloured side.

4
00:00:10,566 --> 00:00:12,294
All player boards are the same.

5
00:00:12,614 --> 00:00:15,025
Every board has the same wall pattern.

6
00:00:16,133 --> 00:00:18,138
Along the top is the score track.

7
00:00:18,458 --> 00:00:21,146
It counts your points, from zero to one hundred.

8
00:00:22,266 --> 00:00:24,037
Put your score marker on zero.

9
00:00:24,357 --> 00:00:26,746
The score marker is a small black cube.

10
00:00:27,866 --> 00:00:29,615
Next, the factory displays.

11
00:00:29,935 --> 00:00:33,157
These cardboard discs hold the tiles that players take.

12
00:00:34,266 --> 00:00:35,781
Two players use five.

13
00:00:36,101 --> 00:00:37,679
Three players use seven.

14
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:39,536
Four players use nine.

15
00:00:40,666 --> 00:00:43,247
Put them in a circle, in the middle of the table.

16
00:00:44,366 --> 00:00:47,652
The space inside the circle is the centre of the table.

17
00:00:48,766 --> 00:00:50,857
Put all one hundred tiles in the bag.

18
00:00:51,177 --> 00:00:52,756
That's twenty of each colour.

19
00:00:54,616 --> 00:00:56,088
Choose who goes first.

20
00:00:56,408 --> 00:00:58,286
That player is the starting player.

21
00:00:58,606 --> 00:00:59,715
Here it's Ana.

22
00:01:00,035 --> 00:01:02,083
She takes the starting player marker.

23
00:01:03,200 --> 00:01:04,906
The marker is not a tile.

24
00:01:05,226 --> 00:01:06,762
It never goes on a wall.

25
00:01:09,083 --> 00:01:12,710
Ana reaches into the bag without looking, and takes out tiles.

26
00:01:13,030 --> 00:01:14,267
That's called drawing.

27
00:01:18,616 --> 00:01:21,923
She puts exactly four tiles on each factory display.

28
00:01:23,033 --> 00:01:25,209
Keep the box lid nearby, empty.

29
00:01:25,529 --> 00:01:27,342
It is the lid of the game box.

30
00:01:27,662 --> 00:01:29,454
Spare tiles wait in it later.

31
00:01:30,566 --> 00:01:31,612
And that's it.

32
00:01:31,932 --> 00:01:33,169
You're ready to play!

33
00:01:34,300 --> 00:01:35,196
Remember.

34
00:01:35,516 --> 00:01:39,697
Everyone uses the same board side, with score markers on zero.

35
00:01:40,017 --> 00:01:44,732
Use five, seven or nine factory displays, for two, three or four players.

36
00:01:45,052 --> 00:01:47,740
The starting player puts four tiles on each one.

37
00:01:48,060 --> 00:01:49,638
Next: taking tiles.
